{
  "programId": "com.digitalarsenal.flows.cellular-network-aggregate",
  "name": "Cellular Network Aggregation",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "description": "Signed isomorphic graph, mounted at /api/v1/cellular. CACHE-FIRST since 2026-08-14 (graph task mod-cellular-aggregate-cache, owner: 'the cell towers should load almost instantaneously'). The ONE $HTQ request now enters at cell-tower-ingest:cache_plan, not at route. cache_plan reads the envelope and picks ONE lane. THE CACHE LANE (the default for an /aggregate read): it emits this dataset's DEFAULT FlatSQL query, hostcap/flatsql-query streams the stored rows back verbatim into foundation/http-respond's body, and a second query over the ingest resume marks feeds cache_freshness, which authors the decision envelope carrying cacheState/freshness/stale/per-provider progress so the UI shows staleness honestly rather than presenting a cached answer as a current one. That path is one SELECT and a byte forward - no provider is contacted. THE LIVE LANE (every other route, and any request carrying REFRESH:true): the $HTQ is forwarded byte-for-byte to route, which behaves exactly as before - it reads the caller's PROVIDERS list and tbsMergeMethod and fans out one hostcap/http-request GET per selected provider; parse normalizes each provider's native payload into reports; deconflict merges them and emits a size-prefixed $TBS record stream. Before the gate existed that fan-out ran on EVERY request and cost ~9s on the live page; it is now the explicit-refresh path, while routine refresh belongs to the cellular-network-ingest timer flow. Exactly one lane emits per request, so two bodies can never race into respond. The catalog and credential routes are finished by cell-tower-credentials, the ONE node holding a credential capability: it appends the node key slot, reports which lanes are configured, and opens/stores a browser-sealed credential. The host owns no schedule, no provider list, no merge policy, no cache policy and no record semantics - it mounts a route and moves bytes.",
